# GetLoadedMap — return master's currently-loaded map metadata + per-AGV
# alignment status. Operator diagnostics for "what's running."
#
# **Why this exists**: an FMS operator needs to answer "is the master
# running with floor1 v1.0 or the staging map?" without grepping logs.
# Pairs with VDA5050Master::load_map_from_config and the master's
# factsheet_alignment validator (Task #39 sub-criterion #2).
#
# Request takes no fields — there is one active map at a time per
# master in V0. Multi-map support is post-V0.
---
# Status enum.
#
# SUCCESS         — a map is loaded; metadata + alignment fields below
#                   are populated.
# NO_MAP_LOADED   — the master is running without a loaded map; metadata
#                   fields are empty defaults; agv_alignments is empty.
uint8 SUCCESS=0
uint8 NO_MAP_LOADED=1
uint8 status

# Map metadata. Mirrors VDA5050 v2.0.0 §6.3.2 / §7.8 State.maps[] field
# names so this can be echoed in State payloads later without a wrapper.
# When status == NO_MAP_LOADED, all string fields are empty and counts
# are zero.
string map_id
string map_version
string map_status        # "ENABLED" / "DISABLED"
string map_descriptor

# Wall-clock time at which the master finished loading the map.
# Expressed as `Time[<=1]` (length 0 or 1): empty when status ==
# NO_MAP_LOADED; single element when a map is loaded. Callers check
# via `.empty()` and access via `[0]` when present.
builtin_interfaces/Time[<=1] loaded_at

# Topology counts (post-parse).
uint32 node_count
uint32 edge_count

# Path the map was loaded from. Empty if the map was set in-memory
# (e.g. via tests or a future ROS-distributed workflow).
string source_path

# Per-AGV alignment summary. One entry per currently-onboarded AGV.
# Empty when status == NO_MAP_LOADED or no AGVs are onboarded.
AgvAlignment[] agv_alignments
